Task 1: Assert status code is exactly 200:-

Method: GET

URL: https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1

Steps in Postman:
1. Open Postman and create a new request.
2. Select GET and enter the URL.
3. Open the Scripts → Post-response tab.
4. Add this assertion and click Send.

pm.test("Status code is exactly 200", function () {
    pm.response.to.have.status(200);
});

Task 2: Validate username and address data types:-

Method: GET

URL: https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users/3

Add this script under Scripts → Post-response:

pm.test("Username exists and is a string", function () {
    const data = pm.response.json();

    pm.expect(data).to.have.property("username");
    pm.expect(data.username).to.be.a("string");
});

pm.test("Address exists and is an object", function () {
    const data = pm.response.json();

    pm.expect(data).to.have.property("address");
    pm.expect(data.address).to.be.an("object");
    pm.expect(data.address).to.not.be.null;
});

Task 3: Validate the Content-Type response header:-

Method: GET

URL: https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/comments/5

Add this script under Scripts → Post-response:

pm.test("Content-Type header is correct", function () {
    pm.expect(
        pm.response.headers.get("Content-Type")
    ).to.eql("application/json; charset=utf-8");
});
